# The commit the lane rule starts after. Everything at or before it is exempt.
# See AGENTS.md, "Classifying a change".
#
# 0662d6e grandfathered the pre-rule gamepad/help/build commits that predate
# consistent lane: tagging.
#
# c06f555 advances it by three commits, on 2026-09-01, for one commit only:
#
#   c06f555 "lib,src: fix the reported orc-desc and status-screen typos"
#
# Its author used the two changed DIRECTORIES as the subject prefix instead of
# one of the six lanes, so the check read it as carrying no lane. The right
# lane was docs: -- an orc Desc string and a "Readyness" status label, prose
# only, no behaviour change.
#
# WHY IT WAS EXEMPTED RATHER THAN REWORDED. The commit was already pushed to
# origin by the time the failure was seen. Correcting a subject line on a
# shared branch means a force-push, and rewriting published history is a worse
# harm than a wrong prefix. Leaving the check red was the other option and is
# worse still: a check that stays red is a check people stop reading, which is
# exactly how bd inc-loa.12 turned one P3 one-liner into noise in every
# session-start report for two days.
#
# NOTHING ELSE IS FORGIVEN BY THIS MOVE. The two commits also skipped over,
# 180113f "rules: ..." and 2777ef5 "tools: ...", both already carried a valid
# lane and both passed. c06f555 is the only commit this exemption covers.
#
# The reason this reached origin at all is that no hook runs
# tools/check_commit_lane.sh -- the rule lives in AGENTS.md and is checked only
# when somebody remembers to run it. That gap is bd inc-er2i.
c06f555
